<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Northcote–Trevelyan Report</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1854">1854</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Northcote–Trevelyan Report of 1854, written by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stafford">Stafford</a> Northcote and Charles Trevelyan, recommended that the British home civil service be recruited by open competitive examination and promoted by merit rather than patronage. Its proposals were introduced gradually, with open competition becoming the norm from 1870, and created a permanent, politically neutral civil service.</p></div>
